  "description": "Continue without an account when the licence changes after the card's press (LK-SKIP, WIRE-CONTRACT-V5 §12.4.2 items 3.6, 3.7 and 5), with key-entry refusals on and a limit of 1. The card issues a code, then the licence joins an account: token repeats the ownership check and answers a flat 403 license_owned with signInUrl, takes no seat and counts nothing. For a second licence another device enters the key after the press, so the limit is reached: token answers 403 key_entry_limit with keyEntries and manageUrl. Each refusal spends its code, so the person presses the card again for a fresh one. Neither is an auth failure: the client keeps its state.",
